        {"h2_html": "What Housecall Pro <em>does well</em>",
         "body_html": '<p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.85;max-width:64ch">Housecall Pro earned its reputation on the operational side of a home-service business, and that strength is real. As described on its site at the time of writing, and worth checking there for current details, it handles scheduling and dispatch with a drag-and-drop calendar, quotes and invoices, card and bank payments, GPS fleet tracking, and a mobile app that technicians run from the truck. For an owner who wants to sit in the driver seat and run the day themselves, it is a capable, well-built platform, and it covers a lot of ground across dozens of home-service trades.</p><p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.85;max-width:64ch;margin-top:1rem">It is worth being clear about what kind of tool it is, because that is the honest basis for any comparison. Housecall Pro is self-serve software: you and your office staff sign in, set it up, and operate it, whether you are a one-person shop or a larger team. It has broadened over the years and now offers its own website, call-answering, and review features too. Those are still tools you switch on and manage yourself, which is exactly right for owners who want that control, and exactly the part some owners would rather hand off.</p>'},
